	)
	(text "Sprite size: 16x16\nBitplanes: 4\nSprite size in bits: 16px x 16px x 4b/px = 1024b/sprite = 1024b/sprite x 8b/B = 128 bytes/sprite\nSprite ROM, 0x8000 = 32768B. 32768B/128B/sprite = 256sprites.\n\naccording to mame charincrement is 64bytes, 64 x 8b = 512b, why?\nlen = total x charincrement = 4b/plane x 64 x 8 = 2048b"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 378.46 67.31 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "99da8ff2-f7c2-4abb-9edf-dcb233984487")
	)
	(text "YPOS[3:0] sets initial position,\nV1,V2,V4,V8 determines which row\nof the sprite is active."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.22 83.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a864c5d8-37de-41e3-a500-733c513fdc57")
	)
	(text "- DM goes from 0..240 during DMA, data written. OBJ RAM is copied from\n  buffer 1 to buffer 2 during DMA.\n- DM goes from 0..127 otherwise\n	Latched bytes, starting from hsync32_n\n	- Byte 0: positions 0,4,8..\n	- Byte 1: positions 1,5,9..\n	- Byte 2: positions 2,6,10..\n	- Byte 3: positions 3,7,11..\nA total of 128/4 = 32 sprites on screen at a time."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 31.75 134.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b0e084d5-7ce4-4c83-96db-cb79988f18b4")
	)
