	(text "When LD goes high it will take in two bytes. The lower\nbyte db0 and higher db1. db0[3:0] will be shifted to\ndsh0[1] and db0[7:4] to dsh0[0].The lowest bit of the\nnibbles will go out immediately and the other bits\nin rising bit order will come out. The same goes for\nthe high byte, but it comes out in dsh[1:0]. The bit order\nis reversed for the nibbles if HFLIP is high.\n\nWhen load is high and clk goes high, HFLIP low:\nQ10 = D14, Q11 = D10, Q20 = D24, Q21 = D27\n\n4 color code bits per pixel\n\nIf HFLIP is not active,\nthe nibble low bit is shifted out first if HFLIP is active:\n\nD[17:14] -> Q10\nD[13:10] -> Q11\nD[27:24] -> Q20\nD[23:20] -> Q21"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 417.83 118.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fa652331-2aa7-495e-8822-1295eb19a27e")
	)
